      {
        "id": 85705,
        "name": "Pydro",
        "username": "Pydro",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/{size}/1844_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-05T02:26:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"ChannginWay\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n ChannginWay:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I'd be interested in the reasoning and timing of the move from Kickstarter to DIY pre-orders for Vengence. I think I've seen bits and pieces on this, but would love to see the decision put in the context of the KS experience from the GTG perspective, and thoughts on future releases.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Vengeance did have a KS, it was part of the Shattered Timeline KS. The whole pre-order thing came much later. They have said in the past that the SotM card game will no longer have KSs, simply becuase it isn't needed. The company is doing well, and they know how their product will sell, and they actually make less selling the games through KS. However, regarding new products, there will be KSs, so that they can see the interest in the product first.</p>\n<p>I am not saying there shouldn't be a blog on this, just giving some info we already have.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:09:28.156Z",
